  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Gusty winds from the northwest during the day\nFriday could lead to isolated power outages.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA weak low pressure system will track across New England and\ninto the region tonight and Friday. A warm front will move into\nthe region first, stretching rain across the Central Highlands\nbefore the surface low moves into the Gulf of Maine. The\nmajority of the rainfall will be across Downeast, mainly\nconcentrated in the coastal areas. There is still some\nuncertainty in just how far north the steadier rain makes it,\nbut we do have pretty high confidence that the highest rain\ntotals will be from Bangor south. Totals could reach around a\nhalf inch, with the best chance of this occurring being right on\nthe coast. Cannot rule out localized amounts around an inch.\nThis is a quick-hitting system, with the steady rain ending by\nabout sunrise Friday. The far north could have a few showers\nFriday morning/midday as the cooler air moves in as well, but\ntotals from this will generally be less than a tenth of an inch,\nif any. Overall, little if any improvement in the drought\nconditions expected with this system.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Gusty winds from the northwest during the day\nFriday could lead to isolated power outages.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nCooler air moving in, with a strong pressure gradient, will lead\nto gusty winds over land during the day Friday. Anticipating max\ngusts 30-40 mph, with about an equal threat areawide. This will\nbe strong enough to lead to isolated power outages. The primary\nthreat is during the day Friday from mid-morning to sunset.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Another chance for rain showers this weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3 DESCRIPTION...\nA weak low pressure system sliding eastward across Southern New\nEngland this weekend will bring our next chance for rain \nshowers. Timing and track of the system remains uncertain at \nthis time with some guidance delaying the onset of rain until \nwell into Sunday or takes the system Eastward into the Gulf of\nMaine. Regardless, minimal drought relief is expected with \nexpected rainfall totals below 0.2 inches across the region with\nhighest totals Downeast.",
